Subject: [PATCH] dynarec/arm64: ADC and SBB load the carry from xFlags without MRS/MSR of NZCV on a CPU with no FlagM

When no native carry reaches an ADC or SBB, the dynarec loads CF (bit 0 of xFlags) into the ARM
carry. On a CPU with no FlagM (ARMv8.0 to ARMv8.3: for example the Cortex-A73 and Cortex-A53 cores
of a Snapdragon 662) it did that with MRS NZCV, BFI, MSR NZCV, and SBB with an EOR before them.
MRS and MSR of NZCV are slow on these cores.

One flag-setting subtract from zero gives the same carry: 0 - (bit 0 << 31) borrows only when
bit 0 is set, and the ARM carry is the inverse of the borrow.
- SBB needs the inverse of CF (ARM's SBC subtracts the inverse of its carry): SUBS of xFlags
  alone. 4 instructions become 1.
- ADC needs CF: EOR of bit 0, then the SUBS. 3 instructions become 2.

The subtract changes N, Z and V too, where the old sequence kept them. They are dead there: every
caller of these six emitters is an ADC or an SBB (SETFLAGS(X_ALL, ...)), which writes all the
flags; the native-flags pass ends a chain of native flags at each instruction that sets flags
(NAT_FLAG_OP_TOUCH); and this branch runs only when no native carry reaches the instruction
(IFNATIVE_BEFORE(NF_CF) is false), so no chain reaches it. The LOCK forms restore xFlags and NZCV
before each try, as before.

No change with FlagM (RMIF), and no change where the instruction takes the native carry.

Why: PD2's D2Lang.dll looks a string key up with an inline strcmp that ends in "sbb eax,eax;
sbb eax,-1", about 25 million times at each game entry, and the first SBB takes its carry from
xFlags. That loop is about half of the time between the realm's join answer and the game's logon,
which the game server limits (issue #17).

Measured on an OPPO CPH2641 (Snapdragon 662, big core at 2112 MHz), 2026-11-10: the translated
loop in the game takes 440 ms at a game entry before and 416 ms after (10 single-player entries
each, the two builds in turn; the ranges 429-448 and 413-424 do not overlap). A native copy of
the loop: 18.5 ns a probe before, 16.7 ns after with the key strings 16 bytes apart.

Tested: an x86-64 program with 455 forms of ADC and SBB (all operand sizes, register, memory,
immediate and LOCK forms, the carry from POPFQ, from a compare before a join of two paths and
through DEC/JNZ loops, each flag consumer by itself) prints the same checksums under Box64 with
this patch as on a real x86 CPU, in qemu-aarch64 with a CPU model that has no FlagM (cortex-a72)
and with one that has it (max), with native flags on and off. A copy of the patch with a wrong
carry fails that test in 119 forms on the model with no FlagM, and in none on the model with
FlagM. Box64's own tests: 35 of 35 pass with and without the patch.
---
--- a/src/dynarec/arm64/dynarec_arm64_emit_math.c
+++ b/src/dynarec/arm64/dynarec_arm64_emit_math.c
@@ -1004,9 +1004,10 @@ void emit_adc32(dynarec_arm_t* dyn, int ninst, rex_t rex, int s1, int s2, int s3
         if(cpuext.flagm)
             RMIF(xFlags, 63, 0b0010);
         else {
-            MRS_nzcv(s3);
-            BFIx(s3, xFlags, 29, 1); // set C
-            MSR_nzcv(s3);      // load CC into ARM CF
+            // no FlagM: 0 - (!CF<<31) borrows only when CF is clear, so ARM CF = CF. No MRS/MSR of
+            // NZCV, which are slow. N, Z and V change too: ADC writes all the flags, so they are dead here.
+            EORw_mask(s3, xFlags, 0, 0);
+            SUBSw_REG_LSL(wZR, wZR, s3, 31);    // load CC into ARM CF
         }
     }
     IFX(X_AF) {
@@ -1151,9 +1152,10 @@ void emit_adc8(dynarec_arm_t* dyn, int ninst, int s1, int s2, int s3, int s4)
         if(cpuext.flagm)
             RMIF(xFlags, 63, 0b0010);
         else {
-            MRS_nzcv(s3);
-            BFIx(s3, xFlags, 29, 1); // set C
-            MSR_nzcv(s3);      // load CC into ARM CF
+            // no FlagM: 0 - (!CF<<31) borrows only when CF is clear, so ARM CF = CF. No MRS/MSR of
+            // NZCV, which are slow. N, Z and V change too: ADC writes all the flags, so they are dead here.
+            EORw_mask(s3, xFlags, 0, 0);
+            SUBSw_REG_LSL(wZR, wZR, s3, 31);    // load CC into ARM CF
         }
     }
     IFX(X_AF | X_OF) {
@@ -1219,9 +1221,10 @@ void emit_adc16(dynarec_arm_t* dyn, int ninst, int s1, int s2, int s3, int s4)
         if(cpuext.flagm)
             RMIF(xFlags, 63, 0b0010);
         else {
-            MRS_nzcv(s3);
-            BFIx(s3, xFlags, 29, 1); // set C
-            MSR_nzcv(s3);      // load CC into ARM CF
+            // no FlagM: 0 - (!CF<<31) borrows only when CF is clear, so ARM CF = CF. No MRS/MSR of
+            // NZCV, which are slow. N, Z and V change too: ADC writes all the flags, so they are dead here.
+            EORw_mask(s3, xFlags, 0, 0);
+            SUBSw_REG_LSL(wZR, wZR, s3, 31);    // load CC into ARM CF
         }
     }
     IFX(X_AF | X_OF) {
@@ -1343,13 +1346,14 @@ void emit_sbb32(dynarec_arm_t* dyn, int ninst, rex_t rex, int s1, int s2, int s3
             }
         }
     } else {
-        EORw_mask(s4, xFlags, 0, 0);        // invert CC because it's reverted for SUB on ARM
-        if(cpuext.flagm)
+        if(cpuext.flagm) {
+            EORw_mask(s4, xFlags, 0, 0);        // invert CC because it's reverted for SUB on ARM
             RMIF(s4, 63, 0b0010);
-        else {
-            MRS_nzcv(s3);
-            BFIx(s3, s4, 29, 1); // set C
-            MSR_nzcv(s3);      // load CC into ARM CF
+        } else {
+            // no FlagM: 0 - (CF<<31) borrows only when CF is set, so ARM CF = !CF, as SBC needs it. No
+            // MRS/MSR of NZCV, which are slow. N, Z and V change too: SBB writes all the flags, so they
+            // are dead here.
+            SUBSw_REG_LSL(wZR, wZR, xFlags, 31);    // load inverted CC into ARM CF
         }
     }
     IFX(X_AF) {
@@ -1496,13 +1500,14 @@ void emit_sbb8(dynarec_arm_t* dyn, int ninst, int s1, int s2, int s3, int s4)
             }
         }
     } else {
-        EORw_mask(s4, xFlags, 0, 0);        // invert CC because it's reverted for SUB on ARM
-        if(cpuext.flagm)
+        if(cpuext.flagm) {
+            EORw_mask(s4, xFlags, 0, 0);        // invert CC because it's reverted for SUB on ARM
             RMIF(s4, 63, 0b0010);
-        else {
-            MRS_nzcv(s3);
-            BFIx(s3, s4, 29, 1); // set C
-            MSR_nzcv(s3);      // load CC into ARM CF
+        } else {
+            // no FlagM: 0 - (CF<<31) borrows only when CF is set, so ARM CF = !CF, as SBC needs it. No
+            // MRS/MSR of NZCV, which are slow. N, Z and V change too: SBB writes all the flags, so they
+            // are dead here.
+            SUBSw_REG_LSL(wZR, wZR, xFlags, 31);    // load inverted CC into ARM CF
         }
     }
     IFX(X_AF|X_OF|X_CF) {
@@ -1565,13 +1570,14 @@ void emit_sbb16(dynarec_arm_t* dyn, int ninst, int s1, int s2, int s3, int s4)
             }
         }
     } else {
-        EORw_mask(s4, xFlags, 0, 0);            // invert CC because it's reverted for SUB on ARM
-        if(cpuext.flagm)
+        if(cpuext.flagm) {
+            EORw_mask(s4, xFlags, 0, 0);        // invert CC because it's reverted for SUB on ARM
             RMIF(s4, 63, 0b0010);
-        else {
-            MRS_nzcv(s3);
-            BFIx(s3, s4, 29, 1); // set C, bit 29
-            MSR_nzcv(s3);      // load CC into ARM CF
+        } else {
+            // no FlagM: 0 - (CF<<31) borrows only when CF is set, so ARM CF = !CF, as SBC needs it. No
+            // MRS/MSR of NZCV, which are slow. N, Z and V change too: SBB writes all the flags, so they
+            // are dead here.
+            SUBSw_REG_LSL(wZR, wZR, xFlags, 31);    // load inverted CC into ARM CF
         }
     }
     IFX(X_AF|X_OF|X_CF) {
